    "Gauss-Newton local tangent covariance is evaluated at a constrained nonlinear optimum; it is not a profile-likelihood interval or an exact nonlinear Hessian result.",
    "At-bound nuisance zero-level parameters are treated as free two-sided tangent directions in the requested formula. Actual allowed local perturbations form a cone, so the usual symmetric interval and standard Gaussian/Wilks interpretation are not established.",
    "Freezing active nuisance parameters gives a different conditional diagnostic, not a justified replacement uncertainty.",
    "All additional free H1 shifts are included among nuisance parameters. Omitting them or fixing all other shifts changes the question.",
    "The row2 diagonal-noise assumption excludes correlated pixel noise, wavelength distortion and calibration uncertainty, model-selection uncertainty, gas-model adequacy and continuum/LSF model uncertainty.",
    "No conversion of D/sigma into a discovery significance is justified by this mathematical check. No alpha or cosmic-time dependence is measured.",
    "A cutoff of 0.01 discards two full-J directions for J004131; its truncated pseudoinverse and nuisance-only projection are different truncations. The discarded full-J subspace has a nonzero target coordinate, so the resulting finite pseudovariance is not an uncertainty for the unrestricted target parameter. Cutoffs <=0.001 preserve full rank for both targets."
